\section*{Summary for Referees}
This manuscript introduces a novel multi-physics simulation engine (SDSE-77) incorporating three non-standard conservation laws. The model is validated against Cassini UVIS/VIMS occultation data and demonstrates significant improvement over classical Newtonian/GR ring models, reducing RMSE from $0.1420$ to $0.0084$ and achieving $R^2 = 0.9946$. Ablation tests confirm that the new conservation laws are necessary to resolve fine-structure opacity anomalies in Saturn’s B-ring. The manuscript is technically detailed, reproducible, and presents a clear empirical comparison suitable for evaluation as a conceptual extension to planetary ring dynamics.

